Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: processor_idle: saturate N1x DRIPS fallback latency

The BIOS305 fallback can expose paired U32_MAX residency and wake latency.
Adding the historical 6610 us adjustment in u32 wraps that latency to6609 us.
Saturate the addition before conversion to nanoseconds, preserving the sentinel
and ordinary finite adjustments. Coordinated and non-N1x states stay unchanged.

---
--- a/drivers/acpi/processor_idle.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/processor_idle.c
@@ -2750,7 +2750,9 @@
 		 * Coordinated mode already supplies its own composite latencies.
 		 */
 		if (n1x && lpi->min_residency == U32_MAX)
-			state->exit_latency += ACPI_N1X_DRIPS_WAKE_LATENCY_US;
+			state->exit_latency =
+				state->exit_latency > U32_MAX - ACPI_N1X_DRIPS_WAKE_LATENCY_US ?
+				U32_MAX : state->exit_latency + ACPI_N1X_DRIPS_WAKE_LATENCY_US;
 		state->exit_latency_ns =
 			mul_u32_u32(state->exit_latency, NSEC_PER_USEC);
 		state->target_residency_ns =
